+
+Bounded source/architecture audit and selected construction:
+
+- A settlement issue that reaches signing or has an unclassified durable
+  outcome may latch `operationAdmissionHalted` in the Node registration.
+  `split-required` remains the only nonmutating, nonhalting control. The room
+  must never publish, retry a suffix, or accept a new public issue on a handle
+  whose issue result is not a success or `split-required` merely because a
+  compatible plan prefix can be read back.
+- Reuse the existing authenticated recovery APIs; add no product API or
+  authority carrier. For genesis startup, privately separate same-store
+  prepare/recover/activate from `prepareDurableRoomState` so the already-open
+  AHE, issuance and journal stores, transport and queue manager remain owned by
+  the session. For successor startup, first await wrapper deactivation and
+  then use `reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption` against the same authenticated
+  stable room-head floor, current snapshot declaration and already-open
+  stores. Deactivation must precede recovery because same-head activation may
+  otherwise return the old registration. Whole-session `shutdown()` is not a
+  recovery primitive: it closes stores, transport and the queue manager.
+- Before an attempted replacement issue, capture the exact prior plan revision
+  and prefix. After a failed/unknown call, only a readback with the same entry,
+  digest and count, prior prefix plus exactly one matching range, one newly
+  allocated chunk sequence, revision exactly `prior + 1`, and the correct
+  partial-null or final-scalar projection is the attempted committed effect.
+  An independently compatible prefix is useful durable truth but is not proof
+  that the old handle remains usable. Quiesce settlement/public issue/close
+  work, deactivate the old handle, authenticate and activate a fresh handle,
+  publish any exact committed outbox row, and resume only the remaining bound
+  suffix. No failure loops on the same handle. Cleanup or fresh activation
+  failure leaves one terminal session and never two active owners.
+- Limit this recovery claim to settlement at room startup, where the room owns
+  either the genesis material or the current successor snapshot declaration.
+  A later hot-adopted successor's close result does not currently expose that
+  declaration and the room's snapshot-store owner is closure-local. Parent f5b
+  must prove authentic current-declaration custody before claiming repeated
+  hot epochs. If existing storage/close seams cannot provide it without a new
+  API, authority carrier or schema, parent f5b stops and reslices; f5b0u must
+  not invent a fixture-only declaration.
+- `lastLogicalTime` comes from the exact signed vertex input. Only an exact
+  `operation.action === "applicationBatch"` with the existing closed nested
+  `batch { entries, version }` grammar may select the final child logical time;
+  an ordinary application operation containing an `entries` or `batch` field
+  retains the vertex logical time. The current test helper's invented direct
+  `entries` grammar is removed rather than supported in production.
+- Validate every existing progress entry's count and digest against the fully
+  rederived ordered operation list before issuing a missing fence. A mismatch
+  issues and signs nothing, leaves lineage/plan unchanged and remains
+  permanently fail closed. Legacy-to-progress plan CAS may originate only the
+  exact zero-chunk record after a genuine nonmutating split; only atomic
+  `transactIssue` appends a chunk.
+- Fix legacy and progress readback without weakening compatibility. An absent
+  selected legacy entry is not linked. Exact progress readback owns sequence,
+  revision, prefix/range and final-scalar checks. Store-level ambiguous outcome
+  classification and room-level recovery must agree; neither digest/range
+  resemblance nor a mutable later plan is sufficient by itself.
+- Remove the room-local copies of the issuance-store count and digest limits.
+  The narrow compatibility amendment is one direct workspace dependency in
+  `examples/v3-room/package.json` plus its importer entry in `pnpm-lock.yaml`,
+  importing the already-public issuance-store constants/helper types. This is
+  no external package, version, runtime-policy or cryptographic dependency.
+  Re-exporting through storage-browser or Node is rejected because it would
+  create a false ownership seam. This exact workspace edge is the sole
+  exception to f5b0t's prior no-dependency-change sentence.
+
+Tests-only RED acceptance, written against existing public/runtime seams and
+not future missing imports or exports:
+
+1. Pin the real `applicationBatch` nested grammar and two ordinary-operation
+   collision controls (`entries` and `batch.entries`); only the genuine batch
+   uses its last child's logical time.
+2. Across memory, Chromium and Node conformance, refuse a legacy-unlinked to
+   nonempty-progress CAS with exact unchanged readback; retain zero-chunk
+   origination and atomic chunk append as the paired controls.
+3. With a progress entry and missing fence, change the rederived operation or
+   transform result and prove zero issue calls/signatures, unchanged lineage,
+   unchanged plan and no fence.
+4. Cover absent legacy entry, wrong sequence, unchanged or surplus revision,
+   skipped/duplicate range, incompatible prefix and wrong final scalar. Each
+   fails closed; the exact one-revision/one-chunk partial and final forms pass.
+5. Through a handle that genuinely latches after signing, cover both no-link
+   and committed-but-unknown partial/final outcomes. The old handle is awaited
+   through deactivation, no work continues on it, fresh authenticated startup
+   recovery owns publication/resume, and every operation appears exactly once.
+   A compatible pre-sign race is distinguished as plan truth but still cannot
+   authorize reuse of an unclassified old handle.
+6. Exercise one real room-to-Node legal deterministic transform whose assembled
+   batch exceeds 65,536 bytes, observes nonmutating `split-required`, and
+   commits at least two progress vertices. A mocked room split and a separate
+   Node split do not satisfy this case.
+7. Cold reopen with the original authenticated source below a supplied
+   `terminalThrough`: open progress exposes it only for digest/suffix
+   rederivation, admitted chunks are not repeated, completion restores normal
+   terminal classification, and another author/scope cannot borrow the
+   override.
+8. Race public issue, close/adopt and settlement recovery; only one active
+   owner survives, the fence stays first, the plan stays monotonic and cleanup
+   failure is terminal. Retain the legacy one-shot and creator-trusted-v1 byte
+   and behavior controls.
+
+GREEN is limited to the previously authorized seven f5b0t production paths,
+the private room recovery/refactor required above, bounded fixtures, and the
+two workspace-manifest paths. No wire/protobuf/checkpoint/anchor/ACL/authority,
+public API, external dependency, cryptography, threshold, timeout or workload
+change is authorized. Run the corrected 35-test f5b0t focused set plus the
+new f5b0u focused set, real Chromium, affected builds/typechecks,
+exact-owner lint/format/diff/source-shape checks, retained issuance/room/
+recovery/creator-successor/active-owner suites and an isolated clean-checkout
+gate. Timing-sensitive retained files may run sequentially, but every selected
+test and unchanged timeout must be recorded; host starvation is not a product
+failure and is not permission to change a threshold.
+
+Because this adds recovery behavior beside signed issuance and one explicit
+workspace dependency edge, one bounded Grok 4.6/high, direct Kimi K3 with
+`KIMI_LOOP_MAX_STEPS_PER_TURN=100`, and Opus xhigh plan review is mandatory.
+Correct P0/P1 in one batch with at most one material confirmation. The final
+combined f5b0t/f5b0u GREEN review inspects the accepted plan, both causal REDs,
